# Component-Driven Architecture

## Pages are Server Components
- All `page.tsx` files: **no** `"use client"`
- Export metadata: `export const metadata: Metadata = generatePageMetadata({...})`
- Pages compose feature components only; fetch data on server and pass props
- Dynamic routes: use `generateMetadata` (`product/[id]`, `blog/[slug]`)

## Feature components handle client logic
- Interactive UI lives in `src/features/<feature>/components/`
- Mark with `"use client"`; encapsulate state, hooks, event handlers
- Keep reusable and self-contained

## Structure

```
src/app/(main)/shop/page.tsx           ← server (metadata + compose)
src/features/shop/components/shop-content.tsx  ← client (interactivity)
```

## Rules
1. Never `"use client"` in `page.tsx`
2. Always export metadata from static pages
3. Move interactive logic into feature components
4. Keep pages thin — import and compose only

## Page template

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next';
import { generatePageMetadata } from '@/lib/metadata-helpers';
import { PageHeader } from '@/components/ui/page-header';
import { ShopContent } from '@/features/shop/components/shop-content';

export const metadata: Metadata = generatePageMetadata({
  title: 'فروشگاه',
  url: '/shop',
});

export default function ShopPage() {
  return (
    <>
      <PageHeader title="فروشگاه" breadcrumbs={[...]} />
      <ShopContent />
    </>
  );
}
```

## Feature component template

```tsx
'use client';

export function ShopContent() {
  // state, hooks, handlers
  return <div>...</div>;
}
```

## Refactor pattern
- Bad: `"use client"` + 200 lines in `page.tsx`
- Good: server `page.tsx` + client `*-content.tsx` in features
